{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbDzZDSguzwUTjayRSon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012qfgpTwY69VjdRJatp1D3i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"C=$(./board post candidate '{\"name\":\"fcc copper (perfect crystal)\",\"family\":\"elemental metal\",\"tier\":\"trust\",\"formula\":\"Cu\",\"structure_source\":\"fcc Cu, a ~3.615 A (Materials Project mp-30)\",\"rationale\":\"Material named in request; posted to carry the premise-check refusal for self-diffusion at 300 K.\"}' --fulfills bffb9b37-bfff-456b-beb9-f1c9a596d5d8:0) ; echo \"$C\"; ID=$(echo \"$C\" | grep -oE '[0-9a-f-]{36}' | head -1); echo ID=$ID\ncat > /tmp/rr.json <<'EOF'\n{\"status\":\"refused\",\"task\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient of Cu in a perfect fcc Cu crystal at 300 K by molecular dynamics\",\"reason\":\"Premise check fails: the quantity is not measurable with MD for this system and condition. (1) In a perfect (defect-free) fcc crystal there is no diffusion mechanism at all: lattice self-diffusion in Cu is vacancy-mediated, and a perfect periodic cell holds no vacancies. Spontaneous Frenkel-pair formation costs several eV and never happens at 300 K (exp(-E/kT) with kT = 0.026 eV). (2) Even in a real crystal at thermal-equilibrium vacancy concentration, Arrhenius extrapolation of high-temperature tracer data (activation energy about 2 eV) gives D(300 K) of order 1e-36 cm2/s (roughly 1e-37 to 1e-35 depending on the D0/Q set used). The equilibrium vacancy site fraction at 300 K is about exp(-1.2 to -1.3 eV/kT), roughly 1e-21, so an MD cell of 1e3 to 1e6 atoms contains no vacancy. (3) Resolution: with ns-scale MD the smallest resolvable D is about (0.01 A^2)/(6 x 1 ns), roughly 2e-10 cm2/s, which is more than 25 orders of magnitude above the physical value. The MSD of a 300 K perfect crystal just plateaus at the thermal-vibration value <u^2> (about 0.02 to 0.03 A^2 for 3 coordinates, Debye-Waller), so a fitted slope would be fitting noise, drift, or integrator or thermostat artifacts. Reporting such a number as D would be wrong. The physically correct statement is: D_MD = 0 within resolution (an upper bound of about 1e-10 cm2/s), while the true value is about 1e-36 cm2/s, set by thermally activated vacancies that MD cannot sample. Well-posed alternatives, which I can run if requested: (a) vacancy-mediated D(T) for Cu: get the vacancy formation and migration energies with the MLIP (relaxations + NEB) and combine them with the fcc correlation factor f = 0.781 in D = f a^2 c_v Gamma, then extrapolate to 300 K with an explicit Arrhenius uncertainty. Validate against measured tracer D at 1000 to 1350 K. (b) Direct MD diffusion where it is measurable: liquid Cu above Tm (1358 K), validating the potential's melting point against the tier1 calibration value, or a cell with a fixed injected vacancy at high T (D_vacancy, rescaled by c_v). (c) Report the 300 K vibrational MSD / Debye-Waller factor, which MD can measure. No MD was run, because no simulation of the stated setup could produce a meaningful value.\"}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/rr.json --parent $ID","description":"Post candidate and refusal run report"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2085,"cache_read_input_tokens":19497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2085,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64e27a0a-7956-4031-ad75-a4528839ae23","uuid":"ee2221ff-32a1-4afd-b464-fd81a8b512d0","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:00:46.641Z","request_id":"req_011CgbDzYscAQ9X1nMqijewf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012qfgpTwY69VjdRJatp1D3i":{"command":"cd /work && C=$(./board post candidate '{\"name\":\"fcc copper (perfect